    },
    {
      "id": "06-vitamins",
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "vitamins",
      "text": "Vitamins barely show up here. Vitamin E is only 1% daily value and vitamin C is 0%. Vitamin C helps the body absorb plant-based iron, so pairing cannellini beans with peppers, lemon, or other vitamin C-rich foods makes nutritional sense. On their own though, the vitamin section is a clear weakness.",
      "textSha256": "d2b755d85784190890cd4b7c85ad130671067ed5a5bafe74ff757cd1e17cccb3",
      "characterCount": 299,
      "byteLength": 278404,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 17.371,
      "audioFile": "/studio-data/uploads/narration/cannellini-beans/06-vitamins.mp3",
      "timingFile": "production/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice/voice-v2-blocks/06-vitamins-timing.json",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "U45JJvqLG4AbLa1N5QBw",
        "historyItemId": "U8xAwN1HGvM4ZlKmGp2N"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice/voice-v2-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3",
      "filename": "06-vitamins.mp3",
      "docsAudioFile": "audio/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice-v2-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3",
      "durationSeconds": 17.371,
      "offsetSeconds": 58.496,
      "wordCount": null,
      "loss": null
    },
    {
      "id": "07-minerals",
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "minerals",
      "text": "Iron and magnesium are both 37% daily value. Iron supports haemoglobin and oxygen transport, while magnesium supports energy production plus normal nerve and muscle function. Zinc is the softer mark at 25% daily value, but that is still useful for immune function and tissue repair. For legumes, this is a genuinely strong mineral section.",
      "textSha256": "a08236e55bc90945272e82777ce9dd89e0b18006f925216252c2348e8e46a846",
      "characterCount": 339,
      "byteLength": 311841,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 19.461,
      "audioFile": "/studio-data/uploads/narration/cannellini-beans/07-minerals.mp3",
      "timingFile": "production/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice/voice-v2-blocks/07-minerals-timing.json",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "AyuxaS36oahsSDHMKsKF",
        "historyItemId": "2Oic3hTBG44LdHmqVZyn"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice/voice-v2-blocks/07-minerals.mp3",
      "filename": "07-minerals.mp3",
      "docsAudioFile": "audio/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice-v2-blocks/07-minerals.mp3",
      "durationSeconds": 19.461,
      "offsetSeconds": 75.947,
      "wordCount": null,
      "loss": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08-pros",
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "pros",
      "text": "The positives first: creamy texture works in proper meals. They blend into soups and sauces while still holding their shape in salads. Cheap dry pantry staple. A bag stores well and turns into several meals for very little money. Mild flavour takes seasoning well. Herbs, tomato, garlic, and stronger sauces all work.",
      "textSha256": "fb0ddab6a549e378832d77e4778513b95b01d2f4d24621ea7337be117bd69a71",
      "characterCount": 317,
      "byteLength": 297631,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 18.573,
      "audioFile": "/studio-data/uploads/narration/cannellini-beans/08-pros.mp3",
      "timingFile": "production/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice/voice-v2-blocks/08-pros-timing.json",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "AO00OSJYm0rREEeAjbIf",
        "historyItemId": "HQtaYnmADi1aiC7QglOX"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice/voice-v2-blocks/08-pros.mp3",
      "filename": "08-pros.mp3",
      "docsAudioFile": "audio/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice-v2-blocks/08-pros.mp3",
      "durationSeconds": 18.573,
      "offsetSeconds": 95.488,
      "wordCount": null,
      "loss": null
    },
    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "The cons next: can be rough on digestion. Their fermentable carbohydrates feed gut bacteria, but can also produce gas and bloating. Dry beans take time and planning. Soaking and a full cook make them less convenient than opening a can. They must be cooked properly. Cannellini are white kidney beans, and raw or undercooked beans can retain a natural lectin called P H A. Proper cooking brings it down to safe levels.",
      "textSha256": "e54ec6bb96fef142d03724386248170000e294d137b588d2c01c5675fb4792a6",
      "characterCount": 417,
      "byteLength": 379968,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 23.719,
      "audioFile": "/studio-data/uploads/narration/cannellini-beans/09-cons.mp3",
      "timingFile": "production/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice/voice-v2-blocks/09-cons-timing.json",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "fuTRk8JfH8vZPy93expS",
        "historyItemId": "vbdUTrXcbl6S0QwoPQ1x"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice/voice-v2-blocks/09-cons.mp3",
      "filename": "09-cons.mp3",
      "docsAudioFile": "audio/episodes/cannellini-beans/voice-v2-blocks/09-cons.mp3",
      "durationSeconds": 23.719,
      "offsetSeconds": 114.141,
      "wordCount": null,
      "loss": null
    },
    {
      "id": "10-closing_summary",
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "closing_summary",
      "sectionKey": null,
      "text": "Best bits are fibre, a low glycemic index, strong plant protein, and excellent minerals. Weak spots are thin vitamin support, possible digestive discomfort, and dry-bean preparation. Best for steady energy, digestion, and budget meals because fibre supports bowel health, while protein and starch make them a substantial staple. Pair them with vitamin C-rich vegetables to improve iron absorption.",
      "textSha256": "d5e454d14775819ed681041889e0e2bd206476c454d0f502a52dbe24a8791fe5",
